post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> Roamgate is installed as /usr/bin/roamgate.
==> To run it as a user service with the packaged unit:
      systemctl --user enable --now roamgate.service
    It listens on 127.0.0.1:8787; set HOST/PORT in
    ~/.config/roamgate/roamgate.env to change that.
    The login token is in ~/.config/roamgate/auth-token.
==> `roamgate service install` writes its own unit to ~/.config/systemd/user,
    which shadows the packaged one; use one or the other.
==> Coming from herdr-gui-bin? /usr/bin/herdr-gui is gone. Remove the old
    service (systemctl --user disable --now herdr-gui.service, then delete
    ~/.config/systemd/user/herdr-gui.service) and see the migration guide:
    https://github.com/powerfooI/roamgate/blob/main/docs/DEPLOYMENT.md#transition-from-herdr-studio--herdr-gui
MSG
}
